          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 3.4: Let us investigate"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.109,
            0.738,
            0.128
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What percentage of total body weight comes from bones and muscles?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.13,
            0.685,
            0.149
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Step on a weighing scale and record your total body weight."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.151,
            0.775,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Use online references or health resources to find average bone and muscle mass percentage for your age, gender, and an Indian body type (these may vary by ethnicity). For example, on average, adult males have about 40 – 50 per cent muscle, and adult females have ~30 – 40 per cent muscle, although bone mass is about 12 – 15 per cent for all adults."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.239,
            0.774,
            0.275
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Multiply your total body weight by the bone percentage and muscle percentage to "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "estimate",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the weight of your bones and muscles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.277,
            0.774,
            0.311
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Record the estimated bone weight and muscle weight, and compare them with your total body weight."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.313,
            0.774,
            0.349
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Compare your findings with those of your classmates and calculate the class average."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.351,
            0.775,
            0.387
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Discuss why do bone and muscle mass differ between individuals, and how do they contribute to the overall body weight?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.396,
            0.587,
            0.416
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.4.1 The musculoskeletal system in action"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.424,
