        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.784,
            0.776,
            0.887
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You may have noticed that some parts of our body can move easily in many directions, while others move only in a single direction. Why does this happen? The difference is due to the types of joints present. A joint is a junction between two or more bones. Joints allow movement but they cannot move the bones on their own. So, what actually causes the bones to move?"
            }
          ]
        }
